# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root.
#
# SSSF runs every agent through the `claude` CLI on YOUR CLAUDE SUBSCRIPTION.
# There are no provider keys to set. Sign in once, outside SSSF:
#
#     claude auth login
#     claude auth status        # should show your subscription login
#
# For a headless box with no browser: `claude setup-token`, then export the
# token it prints as CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN below.
#
# DO NOT SET ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Claude Code prefers an API key over the
# subscription login, so a key here would turn every agent call into metered API
# billing. SSSF strips ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN from the
# environment it hands to `claude` for exactly that reason. If you really do want
# API billing, set SSSF_ALLOW_API_KEY=1 and the key passes through.
#
# Subscription usage limits apply (a rolling five-hour window plus weekly caps),
# and Opus drains them faster than Sonnet or Haiku. A long run can hit the limit
# mid-phase; it then waits for the reset and resumes the same agent session, up
# to defaults.rate_limit_max_wait_seconds (6 h). A later reset fails the run, and
# you rejoin it with --adw-id.

# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# SSSF_ALLOW_API_KEY=1

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_PATH=claude               # claude binary if not on PATH
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
# SSSF_VIZ_HOST=127.0.0.1         # visualizer bind address; the UI has no auth, keep it on loopback
